{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":249045,"duration_api_ms":326842,"num_turns":18,"result":"All tests pass, clippy is clean, formatting is correct. The implementation is fully complete. Let me produce the execution payload.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"All acceptance criteria for tanksim-6e5.6.4 are already fully implemented and passing. The reproduction model uses a 7-factor multiplicative readiness system (temperature, condition, stability, molt_stress, density, TAN, nitrite) that drives spawning rate, hatch success, and egg dropping. All suppression thresholds are named parameters in ShrimpRuntimeParams and the neocaridina_davidi.toml species data file. Snapshots expose `repro_dominant_suppression` identifying which factor most limits breeding. Events (ShrimpBerried, EggFailure, EggDropping) carry cause codes for full traceability. The test file `reproduction_factors.rs` contains all 10 required unit tests plus 2 bonus snapshot-label tests, all passing (12/12). The full workspace test suite passes (0 failures), clippy is clean, and formatting is correct.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verify reproduction logic in shrimp.rs: 7-factor multiplicative readiness (temperature, condition, stability, molt_stress, density, TAN, nitrite) drives spawning, hatch success, and egg dropping\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verify all suppression thresholds are named parameters in ShrimpRuntimeParams and neocaridina_davidi.toml (density_repro_threshold_per_l, tan_repro_threshold_mg_n_per_l, no2_repro_threshold_mg_n_per_l, egg_drop_instability_threshold, etc.)\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verify snapshot exposes repro_dominant_suppression field via dominant_repro_suppression_label() and events carry cause codes (HighAmmonia, HighNitrite, LowOxygen, ChemistryInstability, etc.)\",\n     